  "note": "Municipal election at Warrenpoint, May 1936. Only the West Ward went to the poll, for seven seats; the East Ward was filled without a contest. The contest turned on the question of mixed bathing at the municipal baths. The five East Ward members were returned unopposed (Irish News, 6 May 1936, p. 7; Newry Reporter, 7 May 1936, p. 5). Eight candidates for seven seats; the two at the head of the poll were the candidates who had declared for mixed bathing. 400 of 517 electors voted. The paper prints the second name as 'Cauffield'."
